Z||000000||BroCar 87||08-07-2000||08:58 PM||||If I were to construct a RAM AIR type of induction from the front of the car, would the force be enough to reach the engine in the rear??? I did this to my old Chrysler Laser (turbo), and I could definently tell the difference. BUT the tunnel of air didn't have to travel the whole length of the car before it got to the Throttle Body. So thats my question, Is it going to have enough pressure to get to the tbi in the back of the car to be called a RAM AIR? I know how I would go about constructing it. I am just wondering the LOGICS of it...haha! <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||5
