Z||000012||FIEROCIOUS||08-09-2000||12:27 AM||||My 2 cents.<P>I've kept my mouth shut for months on the validity of ram air concerning Fiero's.<BR>Truth is there is no validity.<BR>Ram air scoops on the side of the car (at least the size of the holley scoop) do not project far enough to be effective, ie. they don't work. The slipstream that follows the body MUST be broken to get any ram air effect! That would require approxematly 10" away from the body. I personaly wouldn't like a ten inch scoop sticking out the side of my car! Holley scoops look cool, but that's about it.<P>As for the tubes running from the front to the rear, with the scoops at the front that is imediate front it would work, however due to the length and tube diameter constraints there would be FAR too much resistance (air friction) to work. <BR>Truth be told it would probably be worse than no ram air at all.<BR>The force required to move the air down the tube would be higher pressure than that being pushed at the opening. It may even actualy starve the engine of air due to a high pressure bubble at the mouth of the tube.<P>What does this mean to you and me? <P>The only benificial improvements that could be made in the form of scoops would be a natica duct (like NASCAR windows and front of a viper.)<P>That hood looks sweet I like it, however it causes drag and if anything pushes air into the front compartment creating more high speed instability. To have a effective scoop on the front would be a GT40 style hood to release the high pressure area below the front. The Trans Am and turbo Sunbird vents work excellent. <P>Hope this helps<P>P.S. at 60 mph 1 lb. boost at 80 2 lb.'s on a good ram air system.    <p>[This message has been edited by FIEROCIOUS (edited 08-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Spyro86SE||08-09-2000||01:10 AM||||ilike the hood but i was wondering is it a functional hood and if it is do u drive on the e way at high speeds because i was told a functional scoop like that is not to good at high speeds because air gets caught in the compartment and starts to lift the front end is this true does any one know for certain what are the benefits for the ram air hood ||||reg||1
