Z||000032||stimpy||08-13-2000||03:20 PM||||Good point Patrick.  To every issue is a challenge.  What I have been thinking about would use tuff bought at the local hardware stor in the HVAC ducting dept. Sure wish I had scanning capabilities to show what I'm thinking. Using a rectangular funnel piece that could be covered with a screen, mounted right where the bottom of the car becomes the firewall ducted to the airbox would funnel a much larger volume of air then the stock opening. <BR>Serious brainstorming question, Patrick, what types of debris shoud one be concerned about? And how would a little creativity nuetralize that problem?<BR>Maybe I'll check out what WalMart has in their hardware dept. Time fo  oilchange anyway!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
