Z||000038||stimpy||08-15-2000||07:25 PM||||Fair enough- but with a screen over the intake, why would the underside of the car be a more hazardous location for an intakeopposed to the front bumper? Sure, water is bad, but with the air intake taking an upward path to the airbox, by the time you are in that deep of water you're floating already! Mud would be a gradual buildup that could be washed at the coinop car wash. Likewise leaves, rocks and wayward kittycats all would be blocke by a sturdy grill. I would most concerned with plastic shopping bags, newspapers, etc that would suck on to the intake...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
